# Jovie — Cursor Agent Rules (thin pointer)

**Canonical instructions live in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (`CLAUDE.md` is a symlink to it).**
Read it, then the scoped rule for your topic in `.claude/rules/*`.

Corrections to guidance that previously lived in this file (it was severely
stale and caused failing PRs):

- **Branch model:** small PRs target `main` via the native GitHub merge queue.
  There is NO `develop`, `preview`, or `production` branch. Never push to
  `main` directly. See `docs/PR_FLOW.md` and `.github/MERGE_QUEUE.md`.
- **Merge queue is hands-off:** green PRs merge on green. Enroll only your
  own PR once it is green. Never dequeue, reorder or re-enroll any PR to jump
  position, yours included, and never remove another PR because the queue is
  slow. Report the wait and keep working; queue throughput belongs to the CI
  owners.
- **No deploys:** never run `wrangler deploy`, `vercel deploy --prod` or any
  other production or infra deploy, or anything that spends money, without
  Tim's explicit yes.
- **Stack:** Next.js 16 + Neon PostgreSQL with Drizzle ORM. The app was
  MIGRATED OFF Supabase — do not write Supabase client code, RLS policies, or
  `auth.jwt()` SQL. See `.claude/rules/db.md`.
- **Auth:** self-hosted Better Auth. Clerk is retired — never import `@clerk/*`
  or add `CLERK_*` env vars. See `.claude/rules/auth.md`.
- **Required checks:** PR Ready, Migration Guard, Fork PR Gate, PR Size Guard,
  Company guards (`.github/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md`). Report exact check failures — never ignore them.
- **Design system:** `DESIGN.md` (Noir Ion) + `.claude/rules/ui.md`.
